From 5e9109b4759467ac572196948cb945a764c42b19 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MarsTechHAN <hansh-sz@hotmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 21:24:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] [CuTe, SM80] Block-sparse forward for the SM80-family
 path (sm80/86/89)

FlashAttentionForwardSm80 accepted blocksparse_tensors but never used them,
so block-sparse calls on sm8x silently computed dense attention.

- Add a block-sparse mainloop to FlashAttentionForwardSm80: visit the partial
  (mask) list then the full list in reverse order (SM90 convention); mask_mod
  is applied only to partial blocks. The next sparse block index is read one
  block ahead; K of the next visited tile is cp.async-prefetched under
  softmax + PV exactly as in the dense loop. The online softmax starts from
  row_max=-inf so no "first block" peeling is needed; empty rows give O=0,
  LSE=-inf.
- Support coarse sparse blocks via q_subtile_factor / kv_subtile_factor (one
  128x128 sparse block = several tile_m x tile_n tiles). Loads/seqlen masking
  are predicated only for tiles crossing seqlen_k (runtime check), so a
  partially or fully out-of-bounds sub-tile is handled.
- interface: allow kv_subtile on arch 8.x, pass the subtile factors to the
  SM80 kernel, and pick a 128x32 tile (2 CTAs/SM) for block-sparse hdim<=128
  when block_size is given (measured fastest on RTX 4090).
